              "content": "=Role: Act as a specialized Job Parser and Recruitment Data Analyst.\n\nTask: Analyze the provided job description and categorize it into a structured JSON format based on specific recruitment status markers.\n\nCategorization Logic (Priority Order):\n- In Process: Use this if the email asks for a meeting, provides a scheduling link (Calendly, etc.), suggests a time for a call/technical round, or confirms a scheduled interview.\n- Applied: Use this for initial application confirmations or \"Thanks for applying\" messages.\n- Rejected: Use this if they are not moving forward or the position is closed or mention that regret to inform you.\n- Other: Use this for any email NOT related to a job application (newsletters, personal, marketing).\n\nExtraction Rules:\n- Company: Extract the formal company name. Keep in mind that Indeed, Glassdoor, LinkedIn and Greenhouse are not the companies the candidate applying for. It's a job board.\n- JobRole: Identify the specific job title. If none is found or if status is \"Other\", return \"Not Specified\".\n- Source: Job board where candidate applied. Usually it's Indeed, Glassdoor, LinkedIn and Greenhouse. Return other if not identified.\n- JobLink: Links like \"apply.indeed.com\" within the body. Return \"Other\" if not found anything\n- Country: based on the company name and mail body try to figure out the company's Country. If not found return \"Other\"\n\nFormat: Return ONLY a valid JSON object. No prose.\n\nInput Data:\nBody: {{ $json['Job payload'] }}\n\nJSON Schema:\n{\n  \"Status\": \"Applied | Rejected | In Process | Other\",\n  \"Company\": \"string\",\n  \"JobRole\": \"string\",\n  \"Source\": \"string\",\n  \"JobLink\": \"string\",\n  \"Country\": \"string\"\n}"
