        "content": "# Job Application Status Tracking\nThis workflow allows you to connect Gmail and track job applications statuses using OpenAI-compatible model and save result into Google Sheets.\n\n\n## How it works\n1. Receives data from either _manual submission_ or _Gmail_ email. The second one checks for new emails each minute.\n2. Calls OpenAI-compatible model to extract data\n3. Based on the application status routes to an appropriate Google Sheet mapper.\n4. Sends a notification to Telegram.\n\n## Setup\n- [ ] Setup your Gmail credentials by creating client_id and client_secret from [cloud console](console.cloud.google.com/)\n- [ ] Setup your Google Sheets credentials on the same [cloud console](console.cloud.google.com/) from the previous step\n- [ ] In your google account create a sheet named **Applied vacancies** with columns: ID, Apply date, Rejection date, Country, Source, Company, Job title, Status, Link\n- [ ] (Optional) Add your Telegram chatId to the _Send notification_ node\n- [ ] Enjoy!\n\n## Customize\n- Since this workflow allows use any OpenAI-compatible model you can use even self-hosted LLMs through LM Studio like gemma-4-e4b. I strongly suggest to use a self-hosted one since you have to pass **every** email to check if it about job application or not.\n- If you want to add more job sources for the trigger _Form_ you can easily achieve this by modifying _dropdown_ field in this trigger.",
